WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.940
So-chan's been acting weird lately.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:04.900
"Weird" how?

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.690
He keeps complimenting me a bunch 
while his eyes dart around everywhere.

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:11.430
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.530
<i>What should I...</i>

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.280
Just tell me where she is!

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:23.210
I can't!

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.130
You shouldn't see her right now!

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.000
You think that's <i>your</i> decision to make?!

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:29.750
Okay, cut.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.190
We're checking the footage.

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:37.260
This script isn't good for my stomach.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:38.130
Huh?

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:41.510
Discover...

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:45.520
Let's go find it together (the future)

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:47.730
There's a glimmer I want to realize with you

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:53.750
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:59.090
Wow...

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:09.710
As though we're weaving together 
our aspiration (Sing a song)

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:14.800
The melody paints a giant constellation

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:19.550
No matter what tomorrow's 
like, it won't betray us

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:25.050
We'll change even the harshest environments

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:27.920
(Some day!) A magnificent Dream

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.460
(Always!) The evening calm's Mild

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:35.900
Aim for distant lands! "Be with you!"

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:37.450
Discover...

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:41.470
A map of the stars (if we follow it)

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:46.870
We'll never look down Smile for you!

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:48.230
Night sky

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:52.370
Let's run across it together (to the future)

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:54.570
There's a glimmer I want to realize with you

00:01:54.570 --> 00:02:00.180
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:05.470
Wow...

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.010
#13 Lies and Formality

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:22.810
So-chan, does your stomach hurt?

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:24.970
I'm okay. It's nothing.

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:28.920
By the way, Tamaki-kun, you're a good actor.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:30.200
Really?

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.530
Yeah, you're really good.

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:34.550
I'm surprised every time we film.

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:36.300
Hmm...

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:41.930
Say, Tamaki-kun... Do you remember agreeing 
to hang out together on our day off?

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:44.800
Yeah. Did something come up?

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:46.680
No, it's not that.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:50.160
There's something important 
I want to tell you then.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.900
What? Are you going to complain?

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.660
On our day off, of all days?

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:56.250
I wouldn't do that.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:59.880
I want to have a nice, calm conversation.

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:03.600
<i>I can't hide it forever.</i>

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.970
<i>This time, I have to tell him about...</i>

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:08.540
<i>Aya-chan.</i>

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.720
Why did you hide it?!

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:14.000
I trusted you.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.210
Wh-What?!

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.960
I'm practicing our next scene.

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:23.720
I'm going to get something to drink.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:32.090
Here you go.

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:35.230
Oh, thank you...

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:38.720
You're IDOLiSH7's Sogo-kun, aren't you?

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.020
Ah, yes.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.490
So-chan!

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.030
I'm coming with you.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:47.400
Good morning.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.340
You're IDOLiSH7's Tamaki-kun.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:51.330
Take this.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:52.000
Thanks.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:55.500
Huh?

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:59.740
You kind of look like my daughter.

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:01.850
Your daughter?

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:04.360
Yes. She's a cute, good girl.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:06.200
She's grounded and mature.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:09.970
You're not the slightest bit like my dad.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:11.830
Do you work for the TV station?

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:15.480
No. I'm here to watch my son work today.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.020
You have a son, too?

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:20.990
Yes. He does well working
 with the adults here.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.350
I'm proud of him.

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:24.740
You're proud of your son?

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:27.520
That must be nice.

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:28.240
Huh?

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:31.510
To have someone like you as a father.

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:34.470
Yotsuba-san, Osaka-san.

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:36.350
Break is ending soon.

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:37.830
Okay!

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:38.860
Got it.

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:39.850
Osaka...

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:42.060
As in Osaka of FSC?

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:45.470
Yes. What about it?

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:47.850
I knew an Osaka.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:50.100
He was a young man in a band.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.660
He passed away a few years ago.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:57.440
Did you know Osaka Satoshi?

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:59.150
You knew my uncle?!

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:01.240
Get on standby, please.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:03.120
So-chan, let's go.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:04.720
Ah, yeah...

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:06.040
It was nice to meet you.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:12.410
That's right. I knew him.

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:19.000
He was a mediocre man who lacked 
the talent to surpass Zero.

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:23.420
So unlike my Tenn.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:26.460
Kujo-san, where have you been?

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:28.680
Around.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:33.680
Tenn, you're a star who will change 
the world in both name and reality.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:40.690
I've been searching for the star 
who would rise above Zero.

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:44.940
I was right when I found you.

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:47.450
I have high hopes for your future.

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:50.050
Zero is a relic of the past.

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:53.950
Don't let the street performances 
or graffiti bother you.

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:56.210
Thank you.

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:02.160
Rise above Zero?

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:09.720
When I finally achieve that dream, 
will you truly be happy?

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:12.680
Everyone.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:14.260
We received a gift.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:18.520
Wow, so many fruits.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:19.810
Who is it from?

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:23.910
Re:vale sent it to us for our final lesson.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:26.450
I'll get some forks.

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:31.730
Re:vale is so considerate 
despite being such big stars.

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:34.550
Even despite things being 
difficult for them right now.

00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:37.640
Momo-san's voice problems, 
the threatening letter...

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:39.630
They're in a pretty tough spot.

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:41.470
I hope Momo-san is okay.

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:43.250
I wish I could do something for him.

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:47.160
Is it Yuki's old partner after all?

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:48.880
But isn't that in the past now?

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:53.780
It'd be nice if there were something 
we could do to cheer them up.

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:56.470
"Hooray! Hooray!" Like that?

00:06:56.710 --> 00:07:01.970
If we remind them of their precious memories, 
they'll remember the bond between them.

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:04.710
Perhaps that would cheer them up.

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:06.780
Their memories, huh?

00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:12.030
I got a good idea!

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:14.500
Guys, lend me your ears.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:18.330
That's a good idea.

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:19.200
Yeah.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:20.080
Let's do it.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:22.410
Riku, nice idea.

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:25.630
Each group can focus on that during practice.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:28.300
Let's get cracking, then!

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.020
Yeah!

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:40.410
All right. Let's take a break.

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.880
Okay. I'll get something to drink.

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:44.210
It's so hot.

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:46.090
So-chan, lend me your towel.

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:46.840
Sure.

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:48.550
Tamaki-kun, do you want a sports drink?

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:49.400
Yeah.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:50.470
And you, Tsunashi-san?

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:51.560
Water, please.

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:55.220
Hup.

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:57.740
No!

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:00.940
If water's not okay, anything else is fine...

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:08.120
I have one of these, too.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:13.880
My dead mom made them for me and Aya.

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:17.190
Why do you have this, So-chan?

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:20.470
Did you see Aya?

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:22.390
Tamaki-kun, there's a reason for this.

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:23.470
Did you see her?!

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:27.560
When? Where?

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:32.150
Why didn't you tell me?!

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:33.190
I don't know!

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:35.600
I only met her twice at the TV station.

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:37.210
I was never able to stop her...

00:08:37.210 --> 00:08:38.800
That's really all?!

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:39.830
Enough, Tamaki-kun.

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:41.480
She said she couldn't see you.

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:42.080
What?!

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:43.880
That's what she told me!

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.420
There's some reason she can't...

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:49.200
But why did you hide it?!

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:51.560
Why the hell didn't you tell me?!

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:56.890
You know better than anyone 
that I'm looking for her!

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:58.300
It's <i>because</i> I know!

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:01.740
I didn't want to bring it up out 
of nowhere and upset you!

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:08.200
If you abandoned this drama you're 
starring in while we're still filming,

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:10.070
you'd damage your reputation again.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.320
So I...

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:19.200
You thought I'd quit working 
again if I heard about Aya?

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:20.620
Tamaki-kun?

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:24.040
I've been doing a good job.

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:31.140
I've been doing my best not 
to trouble you or be late.

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:37.110
You even <i>said</i> I was doing a good job.

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:38.690
But still...

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:42.470
Did you not actually trust me?

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:48.540
You thought I'd quit working 
and stop listening to you?

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:51.810
Is that what you thought?

00:09:55.430 --> 00:09:56.390
Fine.

00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:59.330
Let's continue the lesson.

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:00.240
What?

00:10:01.730 --> 00:10:05.420
I won't abandon my work. It's my job.

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:08.750
Not even if I want to hit you.

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:10.210
I'm sorry.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:12.440
But I'm quitting MEZZO".

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:15.020
You can team up with someone you trust.

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:16.530
You're wrong. It's not like that.

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:19.840
Let's continue the lesson.

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:22.510
I'm not dancing in this atmosphere.

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:24.140
Ryu-aniki...

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:28.140
Sogo-kun, could you leave us for a minute?

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:28.980
But...

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:32.230
It's okay. Let me handle this.

00:10:35.390 --> 00:10:37.540
What have I done?

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:39.710
Sogo-san?

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:44.610
What happened? I heard Tamaki's voice.

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:47.500
I heard shouting. Did something happen?

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:49.500
R&B Group

00:10:49.820 --> 00:10:50.970
What happened?

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:53.330
Tamaki-kun.

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:55.320
I've had enough.

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:57.880
I'm quitting everything 
once this job is over.

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:00.930
Both MEZZO" and IDOLiSH7.

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:03.920
What about your fans and colleagues?

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:05.300
I don't care!

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:08.130
I only started doing this to find Aya!

00:11:08.130 --> 00:11:10.560
Now that I've found her, I don't need them!

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:14.110
People don't trust you <i>because</i> 
you say things like that!

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:19.570
It's not Sogo-kun who's 
sabotaging your hard work.

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:21.910
Don't you think it's that attitude of yours?

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:26.430
B-But still! I worked hard.

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:27.860
I worked so hard,

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:32.210
and he still didn't trust me.

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:38.210
I just wanted So-chan to approve of me.

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:41.970
Tamaki-kun...

00:11:42.290 --> 00:11:46.650
I knew it wasn't true that he admired me,

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:52.550
but I thought if I worked hard enough, 
it might <i>become</i> true someday.

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:54.970
I'd be so happy if it did.

00:11:56.490 --> 00:12:01.990
But So-chan still thinks of me as useless.

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:11.480
No matter what I do, no matter how hard I work, 
he'll always think of me that way!

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:15.370
Can't the same be said about you?

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:16.030
What?

00:12:16.890 --> 00:12:22.350
You're assuming he'll never understand 
you after one disagreement.

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:27.600
Sogo-kun may have done his 
best to understand you.

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:28.600
Huh?

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:31.730
No group members are perfectly
 compatible from the start.

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:35.110
Only by learning to understand 
one another little by little

00:12:35.110 --> 00:12:37.150
do you become the best partners.

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:39.710
We were the same way.

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:42.990
Even TRIGGER?

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:47.510
Yeah. Things were always tense
 in our greenrooms at first.

00:12:47.510 --> 00:12:49.560
I was sighing to myself every day.

00:12:50.210 --> 00:12:52.840
I really missed my friends back home.

00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:54.860
And things are different now?

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.540
How do we seem to you?

00:13:01.970 --> 00:13:06.380
So that firemen story
you told me was about Tamaki...

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:08.960
Why didn't you tell Tama?

00:13:08.960 --> 00:13:11.260
You're his partner, aren't you?

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:12.840
I'm sorry.

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:15.630
Sogo-san was just trying to do
 what's best for Tamaki—

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:16.980
Riku, shut up.

00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:20.440
You need to learn to lean on people, So.

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:22.960
He's not mad that you didn't tell him.

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:26.100
He's <i>sad</i> that you couldn't.

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:29.200
Don't you think of us as your friends?

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:30.580
That's not—

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:34.450
Tama knew you were hiding something.

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:35.460
What?

00:13:35.770 --> 00:13:38.220
He thought something 
happened with your family.

00:13:38.220 --> 00:13:39.890
He was worried about you.

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:41.460
He was?

00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:46.550
Tama thinks about you way 
more than you think he does.

00:13:47.570 --> 00:13:54.350
Since he wasn't close with his family, 
he sees you as a brother. As family.

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:56.260
Family...

00:13:57.430 --> 00:13:58.800
I understand.

00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:03.690
Since you're so kind and helpful,
you're like an older brother to me, too.

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:09.140
How? So is totally a
self-sufficient only child.

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:10.740
Well, so am I, I guess.

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:29.340
Rock Group

00:14:11.020 --> 00:14:13.610
You're prudent and well prepared.

00:14:13.610 --> 00:14:16.640
That's your unique strength.

00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:23.550
But when it comes to us and Tama, 
you don't need to be so careful.

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:27.610
Instead of doing everything on 
your own, tell us about it.

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:29.340
Are we really that unreliable?

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:34.640
I was afraid I'd bother or hurt someone...

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:38.840
That's fine. Having you rely
 on me makes me happy.

00:14:38.840 --> 00:14:40.600
The same goes for Riku and Tama.

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:41.530
Yeah!

00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:43.390
You're not alone.

00:14:43.390 --> 00:14:47.700
You're one-seventh of IDOLiSH7
 and half of MEZZO".

00:14:52.140 --> 00:14:53.000
You're right.

00:14:55.690 --> 00:15:00.250
<i>I need to take responsibility 
for hurting Tamaki-kun.</i>

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:03.000
<i>Uncle...</i>

00:15:03.390 --> 00:15:07.600
<i>How did you make music with your bandmates?</i>

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:13.260
<i>What does it mean to rely 
on people? To have friends?</i>

00:15:15.050 --> 00:15:17.490
<i>If I sit here worrying over it, 
I'm being self-sufficient again.</i>

00:15:17.490 --> 00:15:18.570
<i>I have to change.</i>

00:15:19.090 --> 00:15:21.020
<i>I can't live life alone.</i>

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:27.190
Yeah?

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:29.800
I want to talk. Do you have a minute?

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:33.510
No matter what you say right 
now, it won't change anything.

00:15:33.510 --> 00:15:35.380
You're sure you won't open the door?

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:40.210
Fine.

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:49.350
Wh-What are you doing, So-chan?!

00:15:49.350 --> 00:15:50.380
Are you breaking the—

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:51.930
Huh?

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:55.300
Sorry for breaking your door.

00:15:56.690 --> 00:15:58.330
I'll pay for it later.

00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:03.540
A-Are you sure you're not some 
extremist instead of just a rich kid?!

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:05.770
I'm here because I have a request.

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:06.730
A request?

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:08.940
Please don't disband MEZZO".

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:10.360
Are you threatening me?

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:12.920
I promise we'll find Aya-chan.

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:15.420
So will you reconsider?

00:16:15.420 --> 00:16:17.760
Find her? How?

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:19.110
I'll do anything.

00:16:19.110 --> 00:16:21.540
I promise we'll find her tomorrow.

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:23.720
Tomorrow?

00:16:23.720 --> 00:16:27.670
Oh, right. That's the day off 
we agreed to spend together.

00:16:33.980 --> 00:16:35.320
Good morning!

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:36.930
<b>Re:vale 
Greenroom</b>

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:36.160
Welcome.

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:36.930
Hey!

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:39.850
Thank you for the gift the other day.

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:42.700
I highly recommend the fruits
 from that place.

00:16:42.700 --> 00:16:43.310
Were they good?

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:45.290
Extremely.

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:48.850
Tamaki and Sogo asked us to 
tell you they were good, too.

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:51.820
Tamaki asked for more as well!

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:54.240
Rokuya-san, I don't think 
you needed to tell him that.

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:58.490
If you liked them that much,
 then it was worth it.

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:01.120
Did you come here today just to thank us?

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:03.660
We actually wanted to 
discuss something with you.

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:05.170
What's that?

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:07.820
We'd like our secret concert with TRIGGER

00:17:07.820 --> 00:17:10.440
to be the opening act instead 
of during the event.

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:12.860
We're okay with that.

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:15.630
Wouldn't making that the opening 
act be rude to you guys?

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:17.150
Don't worry about that.

00:17:17.150 --> 00:17:19.030
Do we have your approval?

00:17:19.030 --> 00:17:21.040
Sure. We'll let the staff know.

00:17:22.690 --> 00:17:25.050
We have one more question.

00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:25.770
Iori?

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:28.950
It's about Yuki-san's partner.

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:30.900
Ah. What is it?

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:33.340
Your partner disappeared because

00:17:33.340 --> 00:17:37.160
you were approached by an 
aggressive producer, right?

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:38.240
That's right.

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:41.910
If it's all right with you, 
could you tell us his name?

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:43.890
It may help us figure something out.

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:46.890
The producer's name was...

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:49.130
Kujo.

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:50.460
Kujo?

00:17:50.810 --> 00:17:51.470
What?

00:17:51.930 --> 00:17:55.510
Kujo? You mean Tenn's current dad?

00:17:55.780 --> 00:17:59.050
The man who took Tenn-nii from us?

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:01.550
Yeah, the very same.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.740
He wasn't a good fit for us,

00:18:04.740 --> 00:18:08.060
but he seems to be getting on well 
with Tenn-kun the perfectionist.

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:11.940
Yuki-san, why didn't you choose
 to work with Kujo-san?

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:15.630
Kujo is all smiles, but he's forceful.

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:19.330
No, "forceful" doesn't cover it.

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:20.910
He's more like a man possessed.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:22.450
Possessed?

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:23.990
That injury...

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:33.480
I think Kujo set it up 
so he could acquire us.

00:18:33.930 --> 00:18:35.220
No way...

00:18:36.410 --> 00:18:39.470
Why does Tenn-nii trust someone like him?

00:18:39.890 --> 00:18:41.210
Be careful.

00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:44.060
He's got a dark side.

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:46.680
Commercial ends in 40 seconds.

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:49.110
I'm sorry to do this right now,

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:51.940
but we received last minute 
instructions from the sponsor.

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:54.210
The sponsor? You mean FSC?

00:18:54.210 --> 00:18:55.320
Yes.

00:18:55.320 --> 00:19:01.030
They'd like you to mention this 
during the conversation at the end.

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:02.360
What's this?

00:19:03.130 --> 00:19:05.200
Why would a sponsor want us to do this?

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:06.900
I'd like to know that, too.

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:10.210
This isn't some kind of 
corporate code, is it?

00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:15.210
No, this isn't a code.

00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:16.750
It's fine. We'll say it.

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:20.260
If you say so, Ryu.

00:19:20.650 --> 00:19:23.760
Commercial is ending in three, two...

00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:31.020
<i>The Secret Room</i> special live 
broadcast is coming to an end.

00:19:31.360 --> 00:19:35.050
No matter how many times we do it, 
live broadcasts always make me nervous.

00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:38.610
Since it's still cold out, 
make sure to keep warm.

00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:45.180
By the way, I heard IDOLiSH7's Tamaki-kun 
got sick after accepting a keychain.

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:47.620
Be careful out there, everyone.

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:49.980
After accepting a keychain?

00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:50.660
What's that mean?

00:19:50.890 --> 00:19:53.830
Can you not dig into this topic
 right as we're ending?

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:57.350
Maybe it reminded him of something.

00:19:57.350 --> 00:20:00.260
I think he's caught a bad 
case of... sentimentality.

00:20:01.460 --> 00:20:05.770
And I think <i>you</i> caught a case of Gaku's
 tendency to say cringy things, Ryu.

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:07.930
W-Was that cringy?

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:10.480
No way. It was awesome.

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:11.320
Really?

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:15.430
I think I'll be careful not to 
let Gaku's habit infect me, too.

00:20:15.430 --> 00:20:16.020
What?

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:19.400
Everyone, don't forget to wash 
your hands and gargle thoroughly.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:20.210
Hey.

00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:22.330
See you next week.

00:20:25.470 --> 00:20:27.070
Tamaki-niichan?

00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:32.080
<i>He got sick from a keychain?</i>

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:34.960
<i>He's not well? Why?</i>

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:37.290
What should I do? My brother is...

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:45.180
We're going out into the country 
for a shoot next Sunday.

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:46.680
What's going on?!

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:50.730
I was wondering why you brought me
 to see TRIGGER on our day off.

00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:54.510
What's all this crap about 
a keychain and me being sick?!

00:20:54.510 --> 00:20:57.470
It might make Aya-chan turn up.

00:20:57.470 --> 00:20:59.520
How did you even get them to do it?

00:20:59.830 --> 00:21:01.270
Well...

00:21:01.270 --> 00:21:04.110
<i>You want them to discuss this note 
during the live broadcast?</i>

00:21:04.110 --> 00:21:07.090
<i>Secret Night</i>'s sponsor is FSC.

00:21:08.300 --> 00:21:10.470
The chairman is my father.

00:21:10.470 --> 00:21:12.080
This is direct from him.

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:14.620
I heard you didn't get along with him.

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:17.000
Don't children argue with 
their parents all the time?

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:18.710
But...

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:21.050
This is a directive from your sponsor.

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:24.200
Don't worry. I'll make sure 
you don't get in troub—

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:26.110
Ow, ow, ow...

00:21:26.110 --> 00:21:26.650
Why are you—

00:21:26.650 --> 00:21:29.230
Well, aren't you up your own ass about this?!

00:21:29.660 --> 00:21:32.510
You're pretty stupid for 
someone who went to college!

00:21:32.510 --> 00:21:33.150
Stupid?!

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:33.950
Hey.

00:21:34.630 --> 00:21:36.350
Cut it out, both of you.

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:41.040
That message was for Aya-chan, wasn't it?

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:43.740
No clue why they said they were 
instructions from our sponsor, though.

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:46.710
So-chan's family runs FSC.

00:21:46.710 --> 00:21:47.450
Tamaki-kun!

00:21:47.740 --> 00:21:49.700
What?! Really?!

00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:52.300
Thank you so much for all your support.

00:21:52.300 --> 00:21:55.330
No, I've actually been disowned and 
don't have any connection to them...

00:21:58.580 --> 00:21:59.710
<b>Manager</b>

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:01.960
Hello?

00:22:04.540 --> 00:22:05.160
What?

00:22:06.950 --> 00:22:07.990
Really?

00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:12.100
Tamaki-kun!

00:22:12.370 --> 00:22:14.320
What's going on with Ryu?

00:22:14.320 --> 00:22:15.390
He's taking a while.

00:22:18.310 --> 00:22:19.400
Excuse us.

00:22:19.740 --> 00:22:22.400
Thank you again for another gift.

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:23.770
It's fine.

00:22:23.770 --> 00:22:24.860
Come visit anytime.

00:22:28.580 --> 00:22:29.700
Wasn't that...

00:22:28.660 --> 00:22:33.890
(If you get lost, there's a song here)

00:22:34.810 --> 00:22:39.960
(If you get lost, there's a song here)

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:37.460
Nii-chan!

00:22:38.420 --> 00:22:39.320
Aya!

00:22:39.960 --> 00:22:45.670
We came to understand a brilliant something

00:22:46.390 --> 00:22:51.890
resembling all the light in the galaxy

00:22:52.550 --> 00:23:04.270
Even on days I'm scared, the faint 
warmth I want to deliver won't disappear

00:23:04.270 --> 00:23:10.490
Even if you want to close your 
eyes to reality's reflection

00:23:10.490 --> 00:23:16.170
Come on, let's create an illusion

00:23:16.170 --> 00:23:18.580
The sound of the future

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:22.840
On the curtain of three thousand worlds

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:25.980
We quietly adorn

00:23:25.980 --> 00:23:31.210
Each and every one of us has meaning

00:23:31.800 --> 00:23:35.220
It's the message of the Fantasia

00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:39.740
You're the one who gave 
me the courage to weave

00:23:39.740 --> 00:23:44.940
So I always want you by my side

00:23:55.590 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:55.590 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>"Trigger"</b>
